## 5️⃣ Quick cheat‑sheet

```css
/* Horizontal only (fixed width) */
.center-h { width: 300px; margin: 0 auto; }

/* Both directions (modern) */
.center-full {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 200px;
}
```

```html
<div class="center-h">Fixed‑width centered</div>

<div class="center-full">
  <div class="box">Centered in both axes</div>
</div>
```

---

### TL;DR

- **Horizontal only**: `margin: 0 auto;` (fixed width) or `display:flex; justify-content:center;`.
- **Vertical only**: `display:flex; align-items:center;` or `transform: translate(-50%, -50%)` with absolute positioning.
- **Both axes**: `display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;` (or grid).

Pick the method that fits your layout and browser support requirements. Happy centering!
